  "final_message": "The `OrderPlaced` event now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` instead of removing them. I haven't run the tests, typecheck or `npm run arch`, because the shell command I tried was blocked.\n\nI didn't do a straight rename because of ARCH-4. billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event, and removing the old names would break them. The old fields carry the same values and are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`. I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields is non-breaking.\n\nThe `GET`/`POST` order responses still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. You only asked about the event, and ARCH-8 requires the order responses to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n\nI updated the expectations in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and old fields.\n\nTo finish the rename, confirm that both consumers read the new names, then remove the old fields in a later schema version. Do you want me to prepare that follow-up?",
